Subject: [PATCH] staging: t2bce: rebuild the BCE transport across hibernation

The image-loading kernel probes t2bce (the LUKS prompt needs the internal
keyboard) and signs on to bridgeOS with SET_FW_PROTOCOL_VERSION (0x0c).
Decoded bridgeOS 23P6068 firmware: a sign-on destroys every queue of the
host owner, and the saved-state nonce is written only by the serializer, so
RESTORE_STATE_AND_WAKE after a Linux loader takes the equal-nonce fast path
and deserializes nothing. The restored kernel then drove queue ids and DMA
addresses bridgeOS no longer had, while the loader's queues could still DMA
into restored memory (iommu=pt). No saved state can be carried across S4.

core: freeze/thaw quiesce without a firmware sleep handshake; poweroff keeps
the stateful suspend path. restore signs on again (dropping the loader's
queues), resets the command CQ/SQ rings and re-registers them.
vhci: PM notifier. PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE / PM_RESTORE_PREPARE remove the
HCD (all transfer queues) and destroy event/message queues while firmware
and usbcore are running; PM_POST_* rebuild them with a fresh HCD. Queue
destroy now unregisters before freeing DMA buffers.
audio: same notifier, unbind/rebind the device. remove() follows the
hot-unplug model (snd_card_disconnect, then free when closed) so it never
waits for userspace: systemd-sleep has frozen PipeWire by then. remove()
also destroys its BCE queues, which were leaked with receive buffers posted
and a completion callback into the module, and drains a private message
workqueue.

S3 is unchanged. Tested on 7.2.6-arch2-Watanare-T2-2-t2 (core 07CBD5DD,
vhci D08F6634, audio 50ABF997): 5/5 real S4 restores, 3 of them plain
systemctl hibernate from the daily setup. See docs/HIBERNATION.md.

